LuaSQL MySQL driver: connection options. Upstream candidate.

env:connect() takes an optional 9th argument, a table with:
  connect_timeout, read_timeout, write_timeout  seconds, 1..86400
  ssl     "disable" (plain text), "require" (TLS, no certificate check)
          or "verify" (TLS, certificate and host name check)
  ssl_ca  CA certificate file
Unknown keys raise an error. Without timeouts a lost server blocks the
caller for minutes; the plugin runs queries on the server's main thread.
The ssl option needs MariaDB Connector/C.

When LUASQL_MYSQL_PLUGIN_DIR is defined, every connection uses it as
MYSQL_PLUGIN_DIR. MariaDB Connector/C loads client plugins that are not
built in (e.g. client_ed25519, which cannot be linked statically) from that
directory, from $MARIADB_PLUGIN_DIR or from a path relative to the working
directory. Pointing it at a directory that cannot exist means no plugin is
ever loaded from disk.

